A||||14||fldevel||my fiero is giving me all kinds of trouble this week ...HELP!!||||1||
Z||000000||fldevel||10-05-2000||02:52 PM||||ok ... this just started yesterday ...i was driving along and the engine light came on i dident think anything of it cause the car seemed to be running fine .. so i get to the next stop light and my car started idling down to like 350rpm and then stalled ...so i started it back up and it started ok but it is still idleing real low and almost stalling then it jumps up to like 2000 rpm and slowly settles back to around 500 rpm .. <P>argh .. tranny problems .. now this ??? help!! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||10-05-2000||02:55 PM||||What codes do you get?||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||10-05-2000||03:13 PM||||Sounds to me like it's possibly the MAP sensor....Had one go out once on an 88 Mercury and it acted just like that. Would "surge" between a very low idle and about 1500-2000 RPM.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||10-05-2000||04:36 PM||||i dont have a thingie to check codes .. il have to bring the car to my friend bens house to get the codes .. but ..i might just change the MAP senser to see if that helps any ..sorry im a complete idiot when it comes to electrical systems on cars ...well i know what they all do and how they work just dont know all the tech mumbo jumbo ..just give me a chain saw engine and i can do anything with it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||10-05-2000||04:44 PM||||You know, it is easy to check the codes... I'm sure someone has a thing of what the flashes mean, and to get them, all you have to do is undo the plate over the cig lighter (two torx screws) and you will find a plug type thing. Stick a paperclip so that the bottom passenger side hole and the one beside it are connected (If you looking down from the drivers seat, it would be the two in the bottom right corner).. Turn the car to on (don't start it, just turn it to on) and you should see it start to flash)||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||10-05-2000||04:52 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Features/ECMcodes.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Features/ECMcodes.htm</A>              <P>  *At this address, there is an explination on how to retrieve your codes.  It's simple.  I thought you'd like to read it along with other info. there than to have me post a long one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>p.s.  I hope that address works.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com:0080/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/codes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com:0080/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/codes.html</A> <P>This address has code discriptions.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-06-2000||05:31 AM||||when u geta new map sensor. make sure its the same color code inside the electrical connector. On my 86 there were 4 or 5 diff ones, orange,red,blk,green and blue i think, If u put in wrong color wont work even the tangs on connector wont fit right. I spent a whole day finding this out, all the GM dealers kept giving me a "new" superceeded part that wouldnt work at all. I finally found the right color codes from Autozone.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mattsfiero||10-06-2000||11:04 AM||||Okay two things you said it happens when the car is at an Idle it sounds like the IAC or Idle air control valve depending on what Kind of engine you have depends on where it is. the secound thing is how to check your engine code at home for the cost of a paper clip:<P>1.) be sure the engine is off and the key is not in the on or AC position (Remove the key to be sure)<BR>2.) take a t15 bit and remove the two screws in your ceter consol located at each side of the Cigarette lighter<BR>3.) Take a paper clip and open it and reshape it in a u shape.<BR>4.) if you look under the plate you already removed you will see a little black box that looks like a wire clip...Take the paper clip and insert it between the two bottom passenger's side slots.<BR>5.) Now the car will automaticaly flash a 13 three times in sequence (one short flash pause three short flashes X3)<BR>The following code after this is the code it will flash three times as well and if there are any more it will flash that one next untill it returns to the oriinal code and starts over.<P>Hope this helps<BR>Matt<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||StuGood||10-06-2000||12:30 PM||||Good call... almost...<P>In step 5, you meant it flashes code 12 thrice, not code 13, eh?   ||||reg||4
Z||000009||fldevel||10-06-2000||01:41 PM||||ok .. now can someone give me a table on what all these flashes mean ?? i see all these codes but no table to tell me how the flashes tell me what code i have ..and i just replaced that valve thingie in the throttle body if that helps tward the problem any <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jay||10-06-2000||06:10 PM||||I had a similar idle problem when I had my kit car.  IAC was the problem.  But check the codes.  You can find the code listing in a Hayes or Chilton Manual or go to the link above and print it out.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mattsfiero||10-07-2000||07:37 AM||||Okay if you tell us what the code is I can look it up in my Bible ("Haynes Manual") I do know that the code 35 I believe is the IAC code. But that is the only one I have dealt with. Send the code to me and I will tell you what it is.<P><BR>And Yes stu god my mistake it has been tooo long since I have shot my car for codes...LOL   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@excite.com <A HREF="http://www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero" TARGET=_blank>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero</A> <P>[This message has been edited by Mattsfiero (edited 10-07-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Mattsfiero (edited 10-07-2000).]||||reg||4
